1.What is Compute Engine?
GCE = Goggle Compute Engine IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)
you get virtual machines (VMs) running on Google Infrastructure and you manage
OS and Software .

Image(OS + software for boot disk) + Machine Type (vCPU and Memory) = VM instance

Zonal : A VM lives on one Zone if that zone fails the VM is affected.
Disks : Boot disk and extra disk must be in the same zone as the VM.
Network : Each VM gets a NIC (Network Interface Card) in a VPC subnet with an internal IP
Identity : Each VM runs as Service Account.


Use Cloud Run or GKE when you do not want to manage VMs.

2.Machine Types : Machine Families and types.
A machine type defines the vCPU (Virtual CPU) count and memory of the VM Name
pattern :n2-standard-4 = series ,type . vCPUs.

General Purpose :
E2,N2,N2D,N4 and more
web servers ,apps , dev/test.

E2 is cost-optimized

Compute Optimized : High CPU Performance ,gaming ,HPC

Memory Optimized : M series , very high memory per vCPU ,analytics.

Storage / Accelerated : Storage-optimized high local SSD throughout , AI/ML,GPU

3. VM anatomy and lifecycle:
What you configured when you create a VM ,and what happens during its life.
Boot Disk : OS Image + disk type + size
Network : VPC , Subnet + ,IPs ,network tags.
Identity : Service account and access scopes.
Metadata : key-value data , user script SSH settings.
Availability : Standard , Spot and host maintenance.
Labels : Key-Value tags cost tracking and organization.


Lifecycle : Provisioning -> Stagging -> Running-> Stopping -> Terminated.

4.Persistant Disk.

PD =  Network Attached block storage Data stays even when the VM stopped or deleted.

PD-Standard
PD-Balanced
PD-SSD
Hyper disk
Local SSD


Zonal PD live in one zone. Regional PD replicate synchronously across two
zones in same region.

Snapshots are incremental backups , use schedules for automation.
You can increase disk online , but not shrink.
Boot disk has auto-delete on by default. Data disks do not delete unless you set it.
Encrypted at rest by default . Customer-managed keys (CMK) are optional.

A disk must be in the same zone as the VM. To move a VM to another zone use a snapshot or image.

5.Templates : Images and Instance Templates
Both helps you to create VMs.

Image:
A boot disk template (OS + Software).
Public images : Debian , Ubuntu etc.
Custom images : Your Golden image
Image family points to latest image.

Instance Templates:

Saved VM configuration
Machine type image disk network
Used by MIG (Managed Instance Group) to create VMs.

